      <details class="skin-faq-item">
        <summary>Is red light therapy safe for all skin tones in Dubai?</summary>
        <div class="skin-faq-answer">
          <p>Yes. Red and near-infrared light therapy is generally considered safe for all skin tones, including darker complexions common across the UAE and GCC. It works at a cellular level and does not rely on UV exposure or melanin disruption.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="skin-faq-item">
        <summary>Can red light therapy help with acne in Dubai?</summary>
        <div class="skin-faq-answer">
          <p>Yes. In panels that include blue light, the blue wavelength is used to target acne-causing bacteria, while red light helps reduce inflammation and support faster recovery of active breakouts and post-acne marks.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="skin-faq-item">
        <summary>Should I use red light therapy before or after my skincare routine?</summary>
        <div class="skin-faq-answer">
          <p>Use red light therapy on clean skin before applying serums or moisturisers. This gives the light the clearest path to the skin. After the session, apply your usual hydrating products as part of your normal routine.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

